    "data": {
     "title": "Why a developer reads cards",
     "lead": "I build websites for a living and read Thai tarot and Thai astrology for the people who ask. Both jobs come down to the same thing: taking a system apart until it makes sense.",
     "content": [
      {
       "_type": "block",
       "_key": "k001",
       "style": "normal",
       "markDefs": [],
       "children": [
        {
         "_type": "span",
         "_key": "k002",
         "text": "[Your story goes here. Two threads to tell: the travelling, and the spiritual path, and how they led to the practice.]",
         "marks": []
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_type": "block",
       "_key": "k003",
       "style": "h2",
       "markDefs": [],
       "children": [
        {
         "_type": "span",
         "_key": "k004",
         "text": "How I work",
         "marks": []
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_type": "block",
       "_key": "k005",
       "style": "normal",
       "markDefs": [],
       "children": [
        {
         "_type": "span",
         "_key": "k006",
         "text": "I use two separate practices. Thai tarot, properly called Promayarn cards (ไพ่พรหมญาณ), answers the question in front of you. Thai astrology reads your chart from your date, time and place of birth. Most people get both in one consultation.",
         "marks": []
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_type": "block",
       "_key": "k007",
